Rule 123 (if ndim(x1) and ndim(x2) is 0, data type should be either of them should be comparable types)
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor} |= if ndim(x1) = 0 ∧ ndim(x2) = 0 then ((dtype_(x1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(x1) ≤ 10) ∧ (dtype_(x2) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(x2) ≤ 10)) ∨ (dtype_(x1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(x2) = 0)
>>
Rule 127 (If the tensors have numerical types and both dimensions are greater than 0 then their data type should either be same.)
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor} |= if ((dtype_(x1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(x1) ≤ 10) ∧ (dtype_(x2) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(x2) ≤ 10)) ∧ (ndim(x1) > 0 ∧ ndim(x2) > 0) then dtype_(x1) = dtype_(x2)
>>
Rule 128 (At least one of x1 or x2 should not have string or dtype datatype )
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor} |= (dtype_(x1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(x1) ≠ 12) ∨ (dtype_(x2) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(x2) ≠ 12)
>>
Rule 129 (For the both tensors, all the sizes should be a non-negative number )
{x1: tensor, x2: tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x1) - 1] : if ndim(x1) > 0 then shape(x1, i) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(x2) - 1] :  if ndim(x2) > 0 then shape(x2, i) ≥ 0
